function power_of_two(y)
    return y * y
end
print(power_of_two(6))

<PROGRAM END>


Lua has a native function table.concat(). Which can concatenate multiple strings into one string with given delimiter.

In the previous code, I have used .. operator as concatenation operator. This is because .. is a shorthand operator for concat() function of Lua. But I want to give you a more generic way of string concatenation.


Lua has a native function table.concat(). Which can concatenate multiple strings into one string with given delimiter.



